[{:db/id 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ee934c99-4f27-5203-a0f5-c13e99354b00" "question-d94a5264-18c5-5679-b580-fde7816b3b57"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee934c99-4f27-5203-a0f5-c13e99354b00" :question/id #uuid "ee934c99-4f27-5203-a0f5-c13e99354b00" :question/math-academy-id "q-7630" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2cabfed6c7008b47c3157cca4862d0c2a5b2a2b34e1bb35aeea963b1639af8c.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=1,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-759f0728-d8d2-515a-b991-0560a3f812fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-759f0728-d8d2-515a-b991-0560a3f812fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "759f0728-d8d2-515a-b991-0560a3f812fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d9e0ee02-13c6-544f-b4b9-39031730f3ff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2919188-309d-5e3e-965d-f1e83d98bddc" "answer-d9e0ee02-13c6-544f-b4b9-39031730f3ff" "answer-3c3d7e26-2073-5af5-a3f5-d42d26f20154" "answer-06b57d90-a9ee-54f9-840f-6dfdd3aab51c" "answer-4376677f-9a7f-532f-b66b-ad4902b9c630"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2919188-309d-5e3e-965d-f1e83d98bddc" :answer/id #uuid "b2919188-309d-5e3e-965d-f1e83d98bddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9e0ee02-13c6-544f-b4b9-39031730f3ff" :answer/id #uuid "d9e0ee02-13c6-544f-b4b9-39031730f3ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c3d7e26-2073-5af5-a3f5-d42d26f20154" :answer/id #uuid "3c3d7e26-2073-5af5-a3f5-d42d26f20154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06b57d90-a9ee-54f9-840f-6dfdd3aab51c" :answer/id #uuid "06b57d90-a9ee-54f9-840f-6dfdd3aab51c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}+(y+1)^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4376677f-9a7f-532f-b66b-ad4902b9c630" :answer/id #uuid "4376677f-9a7f-532f-b66b-ad4902b9c630" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+(y-1)^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d94a5264-18c5-5679-b580-fde7816b3b57" :question/id #uuid "d94a5264-18c5-5679-b580-fde7816b3b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-278253" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1a8e0f0c766d2674dbf32feac760baea28418d65565fd6d64dccc6cf3eecd6bf.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-3,4),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-43d267b9-ec22-5b8b-a0c1-af357d98c1d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43d267b9-ec22-5b8b-a0c1-af357d98c1d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "43d267b9-ec22-5b8b-a0c1-af357d98c1d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-23962a06-bb97-5fbd-a080-34dac0fedadd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23962a06-bb97-5fbd-a080-34dac0fedadd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23962a06-bb97-5fbd-a080-34dac0fedadd" :answer/id #uuid "23962a06-bb97-5fbd-a080-34dac0fedadd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4e7ed6bf-1bc2-544f-a2b2-ce9a57e934dc" :activity/id #uuid "4e7ed6bf-1bc2-544f-a2b2-ce9a57e934dc" :activity/title "Equations of Ellipses Centered at a General Point" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049699 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-af068651-d4d2-5cf0-9c59-16a00c0246fe" "step-f12ab8ea-ca60-5bc7-a665-f8bdd2c2c872" "step-bfc51aac-6584-5b70-b332-8fd371dd660d" "step-036e2b13-48e5-5f1c-9ff0-5814ddca4cfd"] :activity/first-step "step-af068651-d4d2-5cf0-9c59-16a00c0246fe" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-af068651-d4d2-5cf0-9c59-16a00c0246fe" :step/id #uuid "af068651-d4d2-5cf0-9c59-16a00c0246fe" :step/content "question-ee934c99-4f27-5203-a0f5-c13e99354b00" :step/next "step-f12ab8ea-ca60-5bc7-a665-f8bdd2c2c872" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f12ab8ea-ca60-5bc7-a665-f8bdd2c2c872" :step/id #uuid "f12ab8ea-ca60-5bc7-a665-f8bdd2c2c872" :step/content 17592186250388 :step/next "step-bfc51aac-6584-5b70-b332-8fd371dd660d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bfc51aac-6584-5b70-b332-8fd371dd660d" :step/id #uuid "bfc51aac-6584-5b70-b332-8fd371dd660d" :step/content "question-d94a5264-18c5-5679-b580-fde7816b3b57" :step/next "step-036e2b13-48e5-5f1c-9ff0-5814ddca4cfd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-036e2